h1(doc, "7.  NEXT STEPS AND TIMING")
para(doc, "The target closing date is February 28, 2025, which leaves eleven business days from the date of this memorandum. The critical path is not the Loan Agreement; it is the four items that determine whether the collateral position exists at all: the survey, the ARC approval, the Triangle Commercial Bank payoff, and the intercreditor agreement. We recommend the following sequence.")
sub(doc, "(a)", "Within two business days: the Bank should request the survey, the ARC approval or certificate of deemed approval, the Triangle payoff letter, the corrected draw schedule and budget, the traced source-of-funds schedule, and the executed intercreditor agreement. Each of these has an external dependency and none can be produced at the closing table.")
sub(doc, "(b)", "Within five business days: the Committee should decide the four open credit questions \u2014 loan sizing, the interest reserve, the Developer Fee, and the net worth covenant \u2014 because each of them changes the Loan Agreement, the note, the deed of trust, the title policy amount, and the budget.")
sub(doc, "(c)", "Within seven business days: Borrower\u2019s counsel should deliver the amended operating agreement, the member consents, the non-consolidation opinion, and the pledge documents so that UCC searches and filings can be completed before closing.")
sub(doc, "(d)", "Five business days before closing: the title company should issue the pro forma policy and the bring-down, and the Bank should confirm the environmental deed notice status and the NCDEQ position on the Restricted Area.")
sub(doc, "(e)", "At closing: no waiver of the intercreditor agreement, the equity deposit, the payoff of the prior deed of trust, or the lien waivers should be permitted. Each of the four is a collateral-integrity condition rather than a formality.")
para(doc, "If the schedule cannot be met, we recommend that closing be deferred rather than that any of the items in paragraph (e) be waived. The record contains too many unresolved inconsistencies for a closing-table waiver to be documented adequately, and each waiver would have to be disclosed in the credit file as an unsatisfied condition.")
para(doc, "We would be pleased to discuss any of the foregoing, to prepare the remaining loan documents on the Bank\u2019s standard forms (the Note, Deed of Trust, Assignment of Leases and Rents, Security Agreement, Guaranties, Environmental Indemnity, Pledge Agreements and Intercreditor Agreement), and to prepare a redline of the Term Sheet conforming it to the resolutions recommended above.")
